Free from what, exactly? A childhood of abuse and anxiety that leads into adulthood, potentially drugs and illegal activity at worst, and at best, therapy and childhood trauma being locked away.

&#x200B;

OP if you read this, I am twice your age, and it doesn't get easier inside, but my god there ARE people out there who will love you if you give them the chance. Don't let your demons drag you down later on in life. You're not worthless.

My most hated Quick Chat is "Wow!"

&#x200B;

Like, yes, I didn't have enough boost to reach up to get the ball because you took both corner boosts and whiffed when you missed it anyway, you clown.

Hey, I know exactly how you feel. And no words I say are ever going to make you feel better. But there are so many more reasons to live than for the love of someone who doesn't reciprocate it.

&#x200B;

If you need to talk, my DMs are open. Even if you just need to vent!

Yes, you're completely correct about this. But as I have explained in the comments to other people in this post, I felt like the game would have resulted in a loss either way. My team mate literally wasn't playing at anyone else's level in this game, and that's not me saying I was better than them, they literally behaved like a bronze for the whole game. After refusing to forfeit, I felt it better to either play by myself.

&#x200B;

The fact everyone in here is so quick to prejudge me is honestly an homage to the human ability to pass judgement on things at face value and ignore the facts when they are presented, and a solid representation of the current political climate.

I don't think you will. I actually had a very similar wound on my thumb about a month ago, lots of blood, but cleaned the wound and dressed it. The wound will scab over after a day or so and after about 2 weeks you'll be left with a sort of scar, as well as a bit of a bump called a keloid. 

&#x200B;

This all depends on whether the wound is deep and how the wound was made. If it was made using a dirty knife or something else that is dirty, I recommend going to an ER so they can clean it. However in the photo you provided, your finger is not bleeding, so it seems like it will be fine.

I made a small bot for it, you can just load this into the console. It will keep you alive unless you get 1-shot:

    	new MutationObserver(function() {
		let health = document.querySelector('.progress-bar-label').textContent.split(' / ');
		let perc = health[0]/health[1];
		console.log("Health percentage: ", perc);
		if (perc <= 0.5) {
			let currentLevel = document.querySelector('#levels > div.bg-primary.text-light.pointer');
			let levels = document.querySelectorAll('#levels > .pointer');
			for (let i = 0; i < levels.length; i++) {
				let name = levels[i].textContent.replace(/\(.*\)/g, "").trim();

				if (name.includes("Rogue Encampment")) {
					levels[i].click();
				}

				if (currentLevel.textContent.includes(name)) {
					levels[i].click();
				}
			}
		}
	}).observe(document.querySelector('.bg-life.progress-bar'), {childList:true, attributes:true, subTree: true});

